          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>According to the Universal Immunisation Programme schedule, within what time frame after birth should the Hepatitis B birth dose ideally be administered?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Within 1 hour of birth</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Within 1 hour is the WHO-recommended time frame for early initiation of breastfeeding, not for the Hepatitis B vaccine.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Within 12 hours of birth</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>While earlier administration is always preferable, the UIP schedule specifies the ideal window as within 24 hours, not 12 hours.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Within 24 hours of birth</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The Hepatitis B birth dose must ideally be given within 24 hours to maximise prevention of perinatal (mother-to-child) transmission of the hepatitis B virus.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Within 72 hours of birth</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Delaying beyond 24 hours significantly reduces the vaccine's effectiveness in preventing perinatal hepatitis B infection, which is the primary purpose of the birth dose.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The correct answer is within 24 hours of birth. This timing maximises prevention of perinatal hepatitis B transmission — a key UIP birth-dose principle."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! The 24-hour window for the Hepatitis B birth dose is critical for preventing perinatal transmission — a high-yield UIP fact."
                }
              ],
